        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1c3f9dc9-091b-5b19-8799-9979e6e131c4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Case\n- Events: 1991 Perfect Storm, 1991 Halloween blizzard\n- Concepts: storm naming, weather patterns\n\nFacts:\n- Over the last week of October 1991, the 1991 Perfect Storm blocked most weather patterns over the eastern half of the United States.\n- Over the last week of October 1991, the 1991 Perfect Storm funneled moisture from the Gulf of Mexico straight northward over the region affected by the 1991 Halloween blizzard.\n- On October 29, 1991, the initial area of low pressure of the 1991 Perfect Storm developed off Atlantic Canada.\n- Robert Case is best known for inspiring the naming of the 1991 Perfect Storm as \"The Perfect Storm.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
